: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong> </strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.5272727272727271; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>23. WHAT ARE ALL TRIPS &amp; ALARMS ARE PRESENT IN PURIFIER?</strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">1. Back Pressure shutdown</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">- this measures the discharge oil pressure and alarms and initiates a shut down when below a set value.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">2. Heavy phase overflow</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">- Oil has a much higher viscosity than water. The heavy phase outlet is led to a small catchment tank contain a float. The outlet from the tank is restricted in such a way that water flows freely but oil tends to back up. This initiates an alarm and shut down</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">3. Bowl not open</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">- this may be done in several ways, typically by a lever switch operated by the discharged sludge hitting a striker plate. The other method is by measuring the motor current, when the bowl opens the bowl speed is dragged down due to friction effects of the discharging sludge and water. The motor current rises until full speed is re-established. This is detected by a current sensing relay</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">4. Water in oil</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">- This found on modern designs which have a detection probe mounted in the oil discharge</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">5. High temperature alarm and shut down</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; text-decoration: underline; vertical-align: baseline;">6. Low control/seal water pressure</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>-</strong></span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">Where control water is supplied via a fixed small header tanks a float switch may be fitted.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>24. WHAT IS DRIVE OF PURIFIER?</strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">THE DRIVE FOR THE CENTRIFUGE IS TAKEN FROM A STANDARD CONSTANT SPEED HORIZONTAL SHAFT TYPE ELECTRIC MOTOR RUNNING AT 1450-1720 RPM WITH AC SUPPLY OF 60 CYCLE. WITH WORM WHEEL BOWL REVOLVES AT A SPEED OF ABOUT 6000 RPM.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">NORMALLY CENTRIFUGAL FRICTION TYPE COUPLING IS USED TO CONNECT THE MOTOR AND THE PURIFIER CROSS SHAFT WHICH HOUSES THE WORM WHEEL ON IT WITH INBUILT WORM.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">THE MATERIAL USED FOR WORM IS HARDENED STEEL WHERE AS THAT FOR WORM WHEEL IS PHOSPHOR BRONZE.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">THE SPINDLE UNIT WHICH IS VERTICAL IS FITTED WITH BALL BEARINGS AND SLEEVE. THE TOP PART OF THE SPINDLE CARRIES BOWL AND THE LOWER IS FITTED WITH CYLINDRICAL WORM (REMOVABLE).  </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">THE SPINDLE IS DRIVEN THROUGH THIS CYLINDRICAL WORM WHICH ITS DRIVE FROM THE WORM WHEEL. THE WHOLE OF THIS ASSEMBLY IS TOTALLY ENCLOSED IN AN OIL BATH AND LUBRICATION IS THEREFORE AUTOMATIC.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 18pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>25. WHAT IS AN ALCAP SYSTEM?</strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•        </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">THE BASIC ALCAP CLEANING SYSTEM COMPRISES:</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q