: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•        </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">AN OIL FEED PUMP, A STRAINER, AND OIL HEATING SYSTEM ARE SUPPLEMENTARY EQUIPMENT TO THE BASIC CONCEPT.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong> </strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong> </strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>WORKING:</strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 72pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><br></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><br></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">Changes in refinery techniques are resulting in heavy fuel oils with increased density and usually contaminated with catalytic fines. These are small particles of the catalysts used in the refining process. They are extremely abrasive and must be removed from the fuel before it enters the engine. The generally accepted maximum density limit for purifier operation is 991 kg/m3 at 15*C.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><br></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">In the ALCAP separation system the separator has no gravity disc and operates, to some extent, as a clarifier. Clean oil is discharged from the oil outlet and separated sludge and water collect at the periphery of the bowl. When the separated water reaches the disc stack, some water will escape with the cleaned oil. The increase in water content is sensed by a water-detecting transducer in the outlet .</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><br></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">The water transducer signal is fed to the MARST 1 microprocessor which will discharge the water when a predetermined level is reached which is 0.2% above the reference value. The water will be discharged from sludge ports in the bowl or, if the amount is large, from a water drain valve.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Verdana&#39;; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">It can be used for oil whose specific gravity is more than 1.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong> </strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>26. WHAT ARE THE BENEFITS OF ALCAP SYSTEM?</strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Times New Roman&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•        </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">CONSTANT OPTIMUM SEPARATION EFFICIENCY</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"><em> </em></span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">IS MAINTAINED SINCE SEPARATED WATER DOES NOT ENTER THE DISC STACK.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> SIMPLE OPERATION: NO ADJUSTMENTS OF THE CLEANING PLANT ARE REQUIRED DUE TO FLUCTUATIONS IN DENSITY, VISCOSITY, FLOW RATE AND TEMPERATURE.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> SINGLE STAGE OPERATION</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"><em>: </em></span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">ONE ALCAP CLEANING SYSTEM REPLACES ONE PURIFIER/ONE CLARIFIER IN SERIES.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> VIRTUALLY</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"><em> </em></span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">NO OIL LOSSES.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-indent: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Comic Sans MS&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">•      </span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> WIDE OPERATING RANGE</span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"><em> </em></span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">AS ANY FUEL OIL WITH DENSITY UP TO 1010 KG/M3/15°C CAN BE EFFICIENTLY CLEANED WITH RESPECT TO WATER AND SOLID PARTICLES. SEPARATION EFFICIENCY IS NOT AFFECTED EVEN WHEN CLEANING FUEL OILS WITH A HIGH WATER CONTENT.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0; text-align: justify; white-space: normal;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>SOME POINTS TO REMEMBER</strong></span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; vertical-align: baseline;"><strong>1. </strong></span><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">Friction clutch is provided as the starting torque is too high so power required is high.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">2. Bowl speed is higher than motor speed.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">3. Pure diesel oil purifier cannot be changed for heavy oil as they don’t have heater.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">4. Pure clarifier cannot be changed to purifier as they don’t have oil outlet.</span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q" style="background-color: transparent; border-bottom: none; border-left: none; border-right: none; border-top: none; line-height: 1.38; margin-bottom: 0; margin-top: 0; padding-bottom: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; padding-top: 0;"><span style="color: #000000; font-family: &#39;Arial&#39;; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" class="CDt4Ke zfr3Q"><br></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></div><div class="Xpil1b xgQ6eb"></div><footer jsname="yePe5c"><section id="h.2ea9c6d37f4eb418_0" class="yaqOZd cJgDec nyKByd" style=""><div class="IFuOkc" style="background-position: center center; background-image: url(https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/sitesv/AG8ngQVSaKaEsXpU2SILiFOUES5HJCq5rYkp0UflQgkOZshmjbwzzQ0Cj6KvdFZYksmDwswT9TxZ72Me6TyMVpNFPCO5M0VhqZ-W8np84If9wX9ZxlYb6a8oKvF5plLPfbXGk3maUxdwkL6419xVd4sevgMKiBSyAc9n0T0K83A=w16383); background-size: cover;"></div><div class="mYVXT"><div class="LS81yb VICjCf j5pSsc db35Fc" tabindex="-1"><div class="hJDwNd-AhqUyc-uQSCkd Ft7HRd-AhqUyc-uQSCkd purZT-AhqUyc-II5mzb ZcASvf-AhqUyc-II5mzb pSzOP-AhqUyc-qWD73c Ktthjf-AhqUyc-qWD73c JNdkSc SQVYQc"><div class="JNdkSc-SmKAyb LkDMRd"><div class="" jscontroller="sGwD4d" jsaction="zXBUYb:zTPCnb;zQF9Uc:Qxe3nd;" jsname="F57UId"><div class="oKdM2c ZZyype Kzv0Me"><div id="h.2ea9c6d37f4eb418_3" class="hJDwNd-AhqUyc-uQSCkd Ft7HRd-AhqUyc-uQSCkd jXK9ad D2fZ2 zu5uec OjC